# rule.require.discoverability

every action a human needs is discoverable from the surface itself — prompted, listed, or shown — never held only in memory or an unlinked manual. recognition over recall (norman; nielsen 6)
test: could a first-time human find the next move without a question or a source read?
how: list the options (`--help`, a usage line, an error that names valid choices) · prompt the required next step · let the label reveal what the control does · link deeper docs inline
```
$ booklesson --board
🐢 which board? one of:
  ├─ foamboard   (beginner)
  ├─ longboard   (cruiser)
  └─ shortboard  (advanced)
```
enforcement: a required step reachable only from memory or source = blocker; an error that rejects input with no note of the valid options = blocker
